text:
starting to like dots, there are some tasks that I prefer to have more supervision, and it's just easier for me to mostly guide and ask dots to use local computer use when needed. 

Also many logins don't work with some form of autofill, so the secure input or 1pass sharing don't work, and I need to take over the bot's computer. Seems like @xai @cursor_ai do not care about local computer use, as they dont have it for @bot or Cursor, but I still think it's still a helpful tool. 

So far using Instinct for day to day tasks, and trying dots/bots for professional/complicated work. Also Bot is faster at replying, but it's not as smart as Dots from what i'm seeing so far. Had to do an online application, and Dots caught way more edge cases, strict requirements, and read through details. Whereas for bot it skipped over the edge cases where I'm more comfortable handling the application on my own.

@thsottiaux some easy wins: it takes 3 clicks on my phone to open dots from ChatGPT app, and there should be shortcut to dictation to it. 

@poteto @ericzakariasson do differnt tier for GrokBot control the intelligence of models used? Right now I just get grok bot default/cua, but previously on Premium+ I think it used Grok 4.6/4.7

